[
 {
  "verse_id": "chunk-v2-n-sastho-k8-11-v28",
  "song": "chunk-v2-n-sastho-k8-11",
  "verse": 28,
  "scope": "passage",
  "structured": true,
  "speaker": "Abhinavagupta (commentator voice)",
  "question": "The ṣaṣṭho vimarśa (the apohanaśakti) closes. Its final concern: the inner appearance\n(antarābhāsa) stands firm in memory, construction, and cognition alike (kārikā 8); it is innate in the\ncognition whose form is the external manifestation, while it stands in memory etc. (kārikā 9); it is\ninnate in the freely-wandering construction (kārikā 10); and hence, from the manifestation of the\nuplifting as wished, knowledge and action are clear for every living one (kārikā 11). Along the way,\nthe freed souls (muktāṇava) and the mantreśvaras are discussed.",
  "premises": [
   "Even in the mokṣa-state, the freed atoms (muktāṇava) — from the parama-śiva, from the\nādi-śiva-ness, from the stain-removal-manifested-śiva-ness — have a distinction. By this part, in the\nduality-side, the freed atoms are indeed distinct, and their manifestation, by the śiva-ness, is the\nun-broken all-knowing; but the three-time-manifestation, being established in the māyīya-knower's\nmanifestation, does not fail to flash for them either (from their all-knowing). The 'ca' says: the\nmantreśvaras, by the authority's exhaustion, even in the mokṣa, in that place, of the other — the atom's\nword-obtaining-cause, the dīkṣā, the vow, the japa, the tapas, the samādhāna, the caryā — by the\ntransmigration, being all-knowing, in the traiyambaka, the knower-ness is not de-valued — so with\nrespect to the mantreśvara too, the eternal is fit. The \"paśvaṇūn\" (the animal-atoms) — the\nanimal-ness only, generally. The \"tattvabhuvanādayaḥ\" (the categories, the worlds) — the ādi includes\nthe bhāvabhūta, the kalā, the mantra, the word, the phoneme. Even the jars and the rest, with respect\nto their own class, are not utterly unprecedented. The 'iti' shows the reason in the future meaning\n(\"not then-created and then-withdrawn\"). The prior-created-ness. The objection \"how, in the dealing-\ntime, is the creation?\" — the prior-view's reasonableness is shown. The \"kintu\" (but) removes the\n\"then how is the creation\" — at that time, by the unity-going; \"tathā sati\" (thus being): per-knower,\nthe jar-appearance and the body-appearance are distinct; but (the vāsanāprabodha-sūtra 1.5.5, and the\n1.5.7 sūtra) — the consciousness-self alone. The objection \"then the knower-distinction is destroyed\" —\nanswered: no (natu); by the prāṇa-puryaṣṭaka, in the triśākhā-and-the-rest-distinction-standing, the\nsameness. And \"the appearance is called the cognition\" — the objection \"the jar-form appearance is the\nknown, how is it the cognition?\" — answered: \"of the knower-operation-form, and\"; \"of the knower-\nstanding-ness.\" The objection \"then by the knower's will, the knower-other-joining, per-moment the\ncreation and withdrawal of the objects and the knowers — how does the maheśvara shine?\" — answered\n(\"sā ca,\" \"evamartham api\"): not only the vṛtti's order-word's pure-form-sequence, but..."
  ],
  "inference": "Decision for L2\nProceed. The argument is understood: the freed atoms and the mantreśvaras are distinct yet\nall-knowing (their manifestation un-broken); the creation is by the unity, per-knower; the appearance is\nthe cognition; and kārikās 8–11 establish that the inner appearance stands firm in memory/construction/\ncognition alike, innate in the cognition and the free construction, and that knowledge and action are\nclear for every living one. The ||6|| colophon closes the apohanaśaktividadhi.\nEOF\necho \"V2N map: $(wc -l < /mnt/HC_Volume_106427611/sanskritree/translations/_stack/ipvv/pilot/pilot_V2N_ARGUMENT_MAP.md) lines\"",
  "uncertainties": [
   "The vāsanāprabodha-sūtra 1.5.5 and the 1.5.7 references — cited; the applications preserved.",
   "The \"traiyambaka\" — the lineage; kept close."
  ],
